The Device List
- Each entry maps to one of The Grand Marina's 3 HYDROLOGIC devices. The name becomes the certificate's Common Name (CN) — this is how the broker identifies which device is connecting.

The Certificate Generation Function
- This is the core of the script. For each device, it:
- Generates a private key for the device
- Creates the certificate with the device's identity
- Signs the certificate with the CA's key
    = Each device gets its own RSA key pair — separate from the CA's key and the server's key. This is like issuing each employee their own unique badge, not copies of the same badge.

.subject_name(subject)
- Who this certificate belongs to (the device)
.issuer_name(ca_cert.subject)
- Who signed it -- the CA, not itself
.public_key(...)
- Embeds the device's public key
.serial_number(...)
- Unique ID for this certificate
.not_valid_before(...)
- Certificate is valid starting now
.not_valid_after(... + 365 days)
- Expires in 1 year
.add_extension(ca=False)
- This is NOT a CA — it can't sign other certs
.add_extension(CLIENT_AUTH)
- Marks this for client authentication — the broker checks this
.sign(ca_key, ...)
- Signed by the CA's private key — this is what makes it trusted

ca.pem
